    "updated_at": "2026-11-14T22:58:47Z",
    "body": "@NeoTech: a suggestion for the Linux packages of v0.20.0. This is a note, not a request to move the tag. The v0.20.0 release has 5 files (Windows, macOS, FreeBSD) and no Linux files.\n\nYou can add the Linux files to the existing release without a new tag:\n\n1. Make a branch from the tag with only the fix of PR #1721:\n   `git switch -c release-linux-v0.20.0 v0.20.0 && git cherry-pick deb88473 && git push origin release-linux-v0.20.0`\n2. Start the release workflow on that branch:\n   `gh workflow run release.yml --ref release-linux-v0.20.0`\n   A `workflow_dispatch` run builds every platform and publishes nothing.\n3. When the `linux` job is green, download its `linux-packages` artifact and attach it to the release:\n   `gh run download <run-id> -n linux-packages -D linux-pkgs && gh release upload v0.20.0 linux-pkgs/*`\n\nThe program code in these files is the code of the tag. Only `scripts/package-linux.sh` differs: the one `%files` line. A local run of the same steps (on Ubuntu 26.04 with rpmbuild) made all four Linux packages, and the rpm holds all 7 icons.\n\nCost: the manual run builds all platforms, about 200 or more billed Actions minutes. Most of that is macOS. Alternative: the Linux packages ship with v0.21.0.\n\nIf you want the mkinney side to do steps 1-3, say so here.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
